1. Unify ad-hoc CLI and schema structures using versioned Protocol Buffer contracts | Currently, introspection models (`CliSchema`, `CliCommand`, `SchemaDefinition`) are represented using custom ad-hoc Rust structs, and JSON payloads are treated as unstructured `simd_json::OwnedValue` (Value). Adopting versioned Protobuf contracts (defined via `.proto` schemas and compiled using `prost`) would align the crate with the workspace's schema-as-code discipline, ensuring robust, backwards-compatible, and cross-platform schemas instead of brittle, ad-hoc JSON structures. | crates/op-inspector/src/cli.rs:37
2. Abstract command execution behind an asynchronous command-executor trait | The `CliParser` and `GCloudParser` directly spin up host processes using `tokio::process::Command` in their helper functions. This tightly couples the adapter logic with local shell execution. Abstracting command execution behind an async `CommandExecutor` trait would allow the inspection adapters to run commands seamlessly across SSH, inside Docker containers, or via remote agents (`kubectl exec`). | crates/op-inspector/src/cli.rs:200
