5. Apply structured tracing spans on recursive introspection methods | The recursive parsing methodologies (`introspect_command_inner`) do not utilize tracing spans. Introspecting complex command hierarchies generates thousands of log messages that become impossible to correlate without a hierarchical span structure. Adding a `#[tracing::instrument]` attribute tracking the active recursive command path would resolve this visibility gap. | crates/op-inspector/src/cli.rs:258
6. Persist the introspective KnowledgeBase utilizing the embedded Datalog engine | The `KnowledgeBase` stores generated schemas and metadata inside an in-memory `HashMap` protected by a `RwLock`. This ensures that all gathered knowledge is destroyed when the service restarts. Transitioning this memory cache to use the workspace's embedded relational-graph database (CozoDB via sled storage) would provide zero-latency persistent knowledge storage and support advanced Datalog relationships on structural command schemas. | crates/op-inspector/src/introspective_gadget.rs:32
